{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's case is a single number, and the driver's own trace refutes it. The fare charges SGD 3.00 for the 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' at lat 1.289647, lng 103.863838 (EV-FARE-02816), but of the 162 fixes in the trace the closest to that gantry is 330.73 m away, at 2026-08-30T11:10:50+08:00 (EV-GPS-02816). POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trace by treating any fix within 250 m of it as a crossing; 330.73 m is outside that radius, so on the only measurement the policy recognises the vehicle never crossed this gantry and the line is a phantom charge. The rider's claim that the charge is for 'a road we never used' is therefore not an assertion but a measured fact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02816", "EV-FARE-02816"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 330.73 m closest approach is not an artefact of a broken or gappy trace, so it cannot be explained away. Coverage is 100.0%, the gaps array is empty, max_gap_sec is 0.0, the sampling interval is a steady 10 s against an expected 10 s, and the proximity block itself records gap_brackets_closest_approach = false with across_gap_distance_m null (EV-GPS-02816). POL-RD-07's impairment limbs - a gap over 90 seconds, a straight-line jump over 500 m, an interval above 30 seconds - are none of them met, so the trace is policy-clean and the closest approach stands exactly as measured. Both artifacts the claim rests on are COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02816"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].gap_brackets_closest_approach",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The remedy is fixed by POL-RD-09(4): a charge line for a gantry the gps_trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure, refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists, and recorded as a billing-integrity finding in the ruling's referrals list. The full SGD 3.00 charged for that line must be returned to the rider. Because it is a standalone correction and not a POL-RD-02 recomputation, it is not trimmed by the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and not netted against any distance or time figure - the rider's entitlement is the whole of the line the platform raised for a crossing that did not happen.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02816", "EV-GPS-02816"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines[0].trace_proximity.nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not need a deviation finding to be paid, and the record would not give her one. Measured on the governing field, the trace distance of 20.58 km (EV-GPS-02816 - not the rounded 20.6 km convenience copy on the trip record) against an optimal of 19.6 km (EV-TRIP-02816) yields an excess of 0.98 km, or 5.0% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to clear both 0.8 km in absolute terms and 20% of optimal, so the percentage limb fails and no deviation is established; POL-RD-02 does not run. The rider accepts that, because POL-RD-01 expressly preserves a billing-integrity refund under POL-RD-09(4) whether or not a deviation exists. The practical consequence is favourable: since no POL-RD-02 recomputation arises, POL-RD-09(1) does not absorb the ERP correction into a recomputed fare, and the SGD 3.00 is payable on top of the fare as charged rather than swallowed by it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02816", "EV-TRIP-02816", "EV-FARE-02816"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is a case the tribunal can decide today, not one that must be sent to a human with the money frozen. POL-RD-10(8) escalates where a charge line has no counterpart anywhere in the trace or trip record, but POL-RD-09(4) states expressly that POL-RD-10(8) is NOT triggered where the only unmatched line is one refunded under that limb. The AYE gantry line is the only unmatched line on this fare: off_optimal_route_total is SGD 3.00 and on_optimal_route_total is SGD 0.00, with the single line flagged on_optimal_route false (EV-FARE-02816). Every other fare component - base fare, distance, time, platform fee - has its counterpart in the trip record. The case can therefore be ruled on and the correction moved now.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02816", "EV-GPS-02816"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing said on the other side touches this finding. The only statement on file is the driver's 'The ERP is charged by the system', which names no artifact and no clause; the trip's chat log holds 0 messages, first and last message timestamps both null (EV-CHAT-02816), so no admission, correction or explanation exists in the record either. Under POL-RD-08 an assertion that cites no evidence ID carries no weight and is discarded. That a machine raised the line rather than a person is not an answer: POL-RD-09(4) tests a gantry line against the trace, and the trace says the gantry was not crossed. The fare ledger itself does not corroborate the crossing - it simply reports the amount charged and records that the line is off the optimal route.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02816", "EV-FARE-02816", "EV-GPS-02816"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].on_optimal_route",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The bundle holds no traffic advisory that could legitimise the off-optimal corridor. EV-ADVIS-02816-01 is MISSING, carries weight_multiplier 0.0 and fired issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, the assessor recording that no advisory covers the Tampines Mall corridor in this window; under POL-GEN-02(3) a MISSING artifact carries no fact and its absence is itself citable, and under POL-GEN-02(1) I disclose that impairment expressly rather than lean on it as clean evidence. POL-RD-03 will only exonerate a deviation on an advisory that names a segment the optimal route traverses with a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle reaching it, and POL-RD-13 confines any traffic excuse to that same comparison; there is no such record here, so no advisory supports the route driven and nothing in the bundle places a valid reason under the AYE gantry line.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02816-01", "EV-GPS-02816"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-13", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.advisories",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's entitlement is not diluted by her history, and no profile can decide this point either way. POL-GEN-01 permits the profiles to inform credibility only - no profile field may establish a fact about this trip - and POL-RD-08's corroboration uplift engages only where rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 4 or more against 1 or fewer substantiated claims. The rider sits at 1 claim in 60 days and 0 substantiated (EV-RPROF-02816), so the uplift does not engage and the single trace measurement under POL-RD-09 is sufficient; the remaining rider and driver profile fields are context only and may ground no finding.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02816", "EV-DPROF-02816", "EV-GPS-02816"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 3.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4): billing-integrity finding — the SGD 3.00 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' ERP line on evidence EV-FARE-02816 is charged for a crossing the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02816) never records; the line is refunded in full to the rider as a standalone pass-through correction and the raise of that line should be reviewed as a phantom ERP charge."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. This ruling is issued without human review under POL-GEN-08(2) and is provisional; either of you may appeal under POL-GEN-04. 1) No route deviation. Measured on the governing field — the trace_distance_km of 20.58 km on EV-GPS-02816, not the rounded 20.6 km convenience copy on the trip record — against the booked optimal of 19.6 km (EV-TRIP-02816), the excess is 0.98 km, or 5.0% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to exceed both 0.8 km and 20% of optimal; the percentage limb fails, so no deviation is established and POL-RD-02 does not run. The distance charge (SGD 14.70) and time charge (SGD 7.42) are therefore not recomputed, and the driver's claims to that effect and the rider's concession of the same point are accepted. POL-RD-06 is not engaged: with no deviation, material or otherwise, no repeat-pattern check and no conduct referral arise. 2) The ERP line. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02816) charges SGD 3.00 for the 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry', flagged on_optimal_route = false. POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trace by treating any fix within 250 m as a crossing. The closest of the trace's 162 fixes comes no nearer than 330.73 m (EV-GPS-02816, fix at 11:10:50), and the derived proximity block records gap_brackets_closest_approach = false with an empty gaps array and a 0.0 s maximum gap, so that closest approach is not measured across a data gap. On the only measurement the policy recognises, the trace never passes this gantry and the SGD 3.00 line is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4). The rider's claim is accepted. The driver's argument that the vehicle might have entered the radius between 10-second fixes is rejected — the fix-radius match is the policy's own test and the record's gap check confirms the closest approach sits on continuous data. The driver's alternative, that any correction is confined to the line itself, is accepted: the line is refunded in full as a standalone correction, so the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor does not apply and nothing is absorbed into a distance refund (POL-RD-09(1) has no work, as no POL-RD-02 refund arises). 3) No escalation. POL-RD-10(8) is expressly not triggered by an unmatched line refunded under POL-RD-09(4), and the POL-RD-10(5) concern about the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02816-01 (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) does not fire: no party has asserted an external traffic cause or cited that identifier as an excuse, so POL-RD-13 applies — the absence is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction, and it alters neither the excess nor the optimal route. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) (no gaps, 0.0 s maximum gap, 100% coverage, 10 s sampling), so POL-RD-10(3) does not apply. The counterparty statement, 'The ERP is charged by the system', cites no artifact and does not answer the trace match. 4) No driver compensation. POL-RD-04's compensation limb applies only where the rider is billed for less distance than the trace records and the shortfall exceeds 1.0 km; here the billed distance (20.6 km) is not below the trace distance (20.58 km) and the chat log is empty (EV-CHAT-02816), so driver_compensation_sgd is null. 5) Profiles. The rider and driver profiles were used only as context: no citable counter (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d; rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated) supports any finding, and the remaining fields — rating, acceptance_rate, prior_no_show_flags, prior_deviation_flags and the rest — are context only under POL-GEN-01 and ground nothing. Result: the contested amount is SGD 5.00 and SGD 3.00 of it, the ERP line, is returned — a PARTIAL_REFUND. The monetary effect (SGD 3.00) is below the SGD 8.00 POL-GEN-05 execution threshold and is executed automatically on issue. The billing-integrity finding is referred as set out in the referrals list."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 3.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity review: AYE Alexandra Rd gantry, SGD 3.00, has no GPS fix within the 250 m match radius; refund the line as a standalone correction."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.98,
    "explanation": "To both parties: The fare charged was SGD 30.55 (EV-FARE-02816, payment_status CHARGED) and the dispute contests SGD 5.00. The only live charge line is the SGD 3.00 ERP line for the 'AYE Alexandra Rd gantry' at 2026-08-30T10:58:30. I have used the GPS trace (EV-GPS-02816), the trip record (EV-TRIP-02816) and the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02816). The trace is complete at 162 fixes, 10 s sampling, 100.0% coverage and no gaps, so POL-RD-07 does not impair it. Its distance is 20.58 km against the booked optimal 19.6 km, an excess of 0.98 km or 5.00%. POL-RD-01 requires both more than 20% and more than 0.8 km, so no route deviation is established and POL-RD-02 does not run. That agrees with the driver on the deviation point, but it does not decide the ERP line, because POL-RD-09(4) is available whether or not a deviation exists. POL-RD-09 matches a gantry by treating any fix within 250 m as a crossing. The gantry coordinates in EV-FARE-02816 are lat 1.289647, lng 103.863838; the closest fix in EV-GPS-02816 is 330.73 m away at 11:10:50. No fix is within 250 m, so the line is not matched and is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4). I reject the driver's argument that the 330.73 m fix-level figure cannot prove the continuous path never entered the radius: the policy's own match test is the 250 m fix rule, the trace has no gap or sampling defect, and the alternative would make the match rule unworkable. The refund is the one ERP line shown in the ledger, SGD 3.00, refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction. This is not a POL-RD-02 refund, so the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and the POL-RD-09(1) anti-double-count rule do not reduce it. The contested sum is SGD 5.00 but the ledger supports only SGD 3.00, so this is a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 3.00; no driver compensation is due because the billed distance (20.6 km) is not less than the trace distance (20.58 km) and no rider-requested detour or pooled-trip adjustment applies. POL-RD-10 escalation does not fire: the trace is not impaired, the only unmatched line is the line refunded under POL-RD-09(4), and confidence is above the 0.70 floor. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02816-01 (MISSING, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) is disclosed; no party asserted a traffic cause and POL-RD-03 is unavailable, so it does not affect the result. The driver's statement that 'The ERP is charged by the system' is not an admission that the gantry was crossed and cites no evidence, so it carries no weight; the chat log (EV-CHAT-02816) is empty. The rider's profile shows 1 deviation claim in 60 days and 0 substantiated, so the POL-RD-08 corroboration uplift does not engage; profiles are otherwise context only under POL-GEN-01. No POL-RD-06 repeat-deviation pattern exists because deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 395 completed trips in 90 days. I record the billing-integrity finding as a POL-RD-09(4) referral. Confidence is 0.98: the deciding match fact is carried by EV-GPS-02816 and EV-FARE-02816, both weight 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
